  "$comment": "The languages Semiont supports. A person reads the interface in one of them, and a resource is written in one of them; the two are chosen independently, from this one list. `code` is the language's code, which names its translation files and its place in a URL. `nativeName` is what the language calls itself: it is what a person chooses from, whatever language the interface is in. `englishName` is what a model is told a text is written in. Every language here has a file in packages/react-ui/translations and in apps/browser/messages-source, and neither holds a file for a language this list does not name; `npm run lint:translations` holds both to it. @semiont/core generates its table from this file.",
